  "note": "kernel-only refresh: same operators and sampling protocol as CB1; startup/example/ALARA legs superseded by P40 identical-data census or unchanged. ACTINV 1.1.2 CRAM solves run selective compensated-residual refinement: refinement is skipped only where every row's componentwise backward error is below 1e-6, no populated component is more than 1e-12 below the largest, and the solution is unamplified; converged iterations exit on a per-row backward-error floor. The 1024-state residual gap vs OpenMC is the cost of the trace-precision guarantee; an A/B build attributes the entire slowdown to solve_refined (commit 35d5448)."
